NNAAMMEE
     mmddiioo — IEEE 802.3 Management Data Input/Output interface

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee mmddiioo

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmddiioo driver provides an interconnection between the Media Access Con‐
     trol (MAC) sublayer and Physical Layer (PHY) entities' control and status
     registers, as defined by the IEEE 802.3 Standard.

     The mmddiioo layer allows device drivers to share common support code for
     various external PHY devices.

     MDIO is one of two signal interfaces that comprise the Media Independent
     Interface (MII) defined by the IEEE 802.3 Standard.  The miibus(4) driver
     provides support for devices that require full MII support.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     miibus(4)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     More information on MDIO can be found in the IEEE 802.3 Standard.

